you're seeing here is real.

00:02:28.365 --> 00:02:30.375
There are board members,
there's presidents,

00:02:30.375 --> 00:02:33.455
there's employees, there's trust funds.

00:02:33.455 --> 00:02:36.925
So these things exist, they
put a lot of pressure on

00:02:36.925 --> 00:02:39.335
doctors and presidents to
make certain decisions.

00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:43.375
- Yes he has autism but he
also has savant syndrome.

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:45.865
Genius level skills in several areas.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:49.655
He as almost perfect recall,
he has spacial intelligence

00:02:49.655 --> 00:02:54.655
and he sees things and analyzes
things in ways that are just

00:02:54.765 --> 00:02:58.555
remarkable in ways that we
can't even begin to understand.

00:02:58.555 --> 00:02:59.845
Those are assets.

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:04.285
Undeniable assets for any
doctor, particularly a surgeon.

00:03:04.285 --> 00:03:06.485
- I'm not gonna lie I agree
with the president on that.

00:03:06.485 --> 00:03:10.145
As a surgeon, it's more important
to have very good spacial

00:03:10.145 --> 00:03:12.585
ability, to be able to
have perfect recall,

00:03:12.585 --> 00:03:16.615
to understand the anatomy
perfectly than it probably is

00:03:16.615 --> 00:03:19.695
to explain the complexity
of a specific case

00:03:19.695 --> 00:03:21.305
and to be able to
communicate well with people.

00:03:21.305 --> 00:03:23.125
Most the time when you're a surgeon

00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:24.685
your patient is not awake.

00:03:24.685 --> 00:03:27.005
With that being said, I think
it is still important for

00:03:27.005 --> 00:03:30.235
surgeons to be able to improve
their communication skills.

00:03:30.235 --> 00:03:32.055
To be able to talk to patients,

00:03:32.055 --> 00:03:34.765
help them understand the risks
and benefits of operations

00:03:34.765 --> 00:03:36.595
and make sure that they
don't force patients

00:03:36.595 --> 00:03:38.275
to go under the knife
when they don't have to.

