00:04:35.155 --> 00:04:38.845
Venous distention is caused
by increased intrathoracic

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.795
pressure inside the chest cavity.

00:04:40.795 --> 00:04:44.335
He's basically saying the
veins in the arms are swollen.

00:04:44.335 --> 00:04:46.495
So he thinks there's some
extra pressure going on

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:48.805
inside the chest cavity.

00:04:48.805 --> 00:04:51.755
It can be because of Cardiac Tamponade.

00:04:51.755 --> 00:04:53.875
Which means that there's blood usually

00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:57.315
in a traumatic sense like this
inside the paracardial tissue

00:04:57.315 --> 00:04:58.865
which is the lining of the heart.

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.795
And there could be blood in
there and it makes the heart

00:05:00.795 --> 00:05:02.208
unable to beat properly.

00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:05.715
- The veins in the boy's
left arm are popping.

00:05:05.715 --> 00:05:06.787
- Is that bad?

00:05:06.787 --> 00:05:08.085
- I don't see.

00:05:08.085 --> 00:05:09.132
- Intrathoracic pressure.

00:05:09.132 --> 00:05:11.315
- Now if his chest is
rising he's breathing.

00:05:11.315 --> 00:05:14.845
- The chest is moving paradoxically.

00:05:14.845 --> 00:05:19.245
- Paradoxical chest
movement is a consequence of

00:05:19.245 --> 00:05:20.755
something known as flail chest.

00:05:20.755 --> 00:05:23.975
If you get a trauma where
a section of your ribs

00:05:23.975 --> 00:05:26.225
break from the rest of the ribs.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:28.855
That part of the ribcage doesn't
move normally when you take

00:05:28.855 --> 00:05:31.151
deep breath in and deep breath out.

00:05:31.151 --> 00:05:33.075
So the chest sort of moves paradoxically.

00:05:33.075 --> 00:05:34.625
That's what he's talking about.

00:05:37.465 --> 00:05:40.075
What happens during a
pneumothorax one of the lungs

00:05:40.075 --> 00:05:42.505
collapses or sometimes
both of the lungs collapse.

00:05:42.505 --> 00:05:45.095
And you can't oxygenate that
area meaning that when you

00:05:45.095 --> 00:05:47.215
breathe no oxygen goes to that area.

00:05:47.215 --> 00:05:48.925
It causes increased pressure.

00:05:48.925 --> 00:05:51.015
The life saving treatment
for this is to literally

00:05:51.015 --> 00:05:53.875
insert a needle in order to
release some of that pressure.

00:05:53.875 --> 00:05:56.029
- Who here has a sharp knife?

00:05:56.029 --> 00:05:56.999
