that makes it difficult

00:11:20.445 --> 00:11:22.625
for that heart to beat and
you get cardiac tamponade.

00:11:22.625 --> 00:11:24.618
That's what I was talking about earlier.

00:11:26.991 --> 00:11:27.824
- Again.

00:11:29.575 --> 00:11:30.408
Again.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:32.513
There.

00:11:33.585 --> 00:11:34.948
- Looks normal to me.

00:11:34.948 --> 00:11:36.165
- It's not normal.

00:11:36.165 --> 00:11:38.095
- Four doctors are looking at a scan.

00:11:38.095 --> 00:11:40.225
They don't believe there to be an issue.

00:11:40.225 --> 00:11:42.335
This guy comes in, sees
an issue with the scan

00:11:42.335 --> 00:11:44.625
that no one else sees
and now all of a sudden

00:11:44.625 --> 00:11:45.655
there starting to believe him

00:11:45.655 --> 00:11:47.335
that maybe it could be that.

00:11:47.335 --> 00:11:50.165
If your looking at the scan
it either is or it isn't.

00:11:50.165 --> 00:11:52.095
I don't know what they're debating about

00:11:52.095 --> 00:11:54.615
the concavity that's
open to interpretation.

00:11:54.615 --> 00:11:57.005
I've never seen a situation like this.

00:11:57.005 --> 00:11:59.255
- The YouTube clip already
has over 200,000 views.

00:11:59.255 --> 00:12:01.345
- That's pretty good 200,000 views.

00:12:01.345 --> 00:12:05.245
The more I think about what
he did there in the airport

00:12:05.245 --> 00:12:07.625
the more I think it's inappropriate.

00:12:07.625 --> 00:12:09.435
There is a good samaritan law that's

00:12:09.435 --> 00:12:11.445
in place to help with basic emergencies.

00:12:11.445 --> 00:12:14.775
Pulling someone out of a
burning car and in the process

00:12:14.775 --> 00:12:16.475
you hurt their back trying to save them.

00:12:16.475 --> 00:12:18.615
But performing an
advanced medical procedure

00:12:18.615 --> 00:12:19.885
like putting in a chest tube,

00:12:19.885 --> 00:12:21.915
especially a makeshift
test tube like that.

00:12:21.915 --> 00:12:26.185
Man unless he saves the
boy and it's 100% safe

00:12:26.185 --> 00:12:28.515
there's gonna be malpractice and lawyers

00:12:28.515 --> 00:12:29.615
involved in that case.

00:12:30.731 --> 00:12:33.898
(slowly rising music)

00:12:39.985 --> 00:12:41.835
- The good doctor strikes again.

00:12:41.835 --> 00:12:44.875
- You saved that boy's life.

00:12:44.875 --> 00:12:46.505
- Well good.

00:12:46.505 --> 00:12:49.398
His name is Adam. Traumatic pneumothorax.

00:12:50.815 --> 00:12:51.648
I'm hungry.

00:12:52.823 --> 00:12:53.755
- Shuan.

00:12:53.755 --> 00:12:56.668
Dr. Melendez's team is going into surgery.

00:12:58.335 --> 00:13:00.468
I mean if you're interested.

00:13:01.975 --> 00:13:04.405
- I mean how bout getting
him to sign all the paperwork

00:13:04.405 --> 00:13:06.955
and disclosures and HIPPA forms

00:13:06.955 --> 00:13:09.865
and making sure he has identification.

00:13:09.865 --> 00:13:10.998
Put your mask on.

00:13:12.295 --> 00:13:13.795
Put your mask on Shaun.

00:13:13.795 --> 00:13:15.995
- I saw a lot of surgeons
in medical school.

00:13:18.255 --> 00:13:20.195
You're much better than them.

00:13:20.195 --> 00:13:21.745
I have a lot to learn from you.

00:13:29.175 --> 00:13:30.966
You're very arrogant.

00:13:30.966 --> 00:13:32.385
- (laughing) Matter of fact.

00:13:32.385 --> 00:13:34.635
- You think that helps
you be a good surgeon?

00:13:36.385 --> 00:13:37.835
Does it hurt you as a person?

00:13:40.435 --> 00:13:41.268
Is it worth it?

00:13:42.549 --> 00:13:45.716
(slow dramatic music)

00:13:50.135 --> 00:13:54.075
- And there you have it first
episode of the Good Doctor.

00:13:54.075 --> 00:13:56.445
Things I definitely
enjoyed about the show.

00:13:56.445 --> 00:13:58.615
Number one it's fairly medically accurate.

00:13:58.615 --> 00:14:00.535
The drama in the show is interesting.

00:14:00.535 --> 00:14:02.605
It kept my attention and I wanted to see

00:14:02.605 --> 00:14:03.645
more of what would happen.

00:14:03.645 --> 00:14:06.029
I really dig the fact that
it gave an inside look

00:14:06.029 --> 00:14:09.495
into how hard living with autism can be.

00:14:09.495 --> 00:14:11.845
You know you could have abusive family,

00:14:11.845 --> 00:14:13.705
you have bullying that's happening.

00:14:13.705 --> 00:14:15.815
Dealing with autism is
a difficult situation

00:14:15.815 --> 00:14:17.775
and I appreciate that
the show highlights that.

00:14:17.775 --> 00:14:21.755
I will say however that
they almost make him look

00:14:21.755 --> 00:14:23.525
super human and that's not realistic.

00:14:23.525 --> 00:14:25.595
So that's definitely a con in my book.

00:14:25.595 --> 00:14:27.975
But I understand that
they need that factor

00:14:27.975 --> 00:14:29.035
to make the show work.

00:14:29.035 --> 00:14:31.795
There wasn't that much
medical stuff to comment on.

00:14:31.795 --> 00:14:34.205
It was a lot about developing
him as a character.

00:14:34.205 --> 00:14:36.265
If you know a better episode where there

00:14:36.265 --> 00:14:39.115
were more medical situations
that I can comment on,

00:14:39.115 --> 00:14:40.505
let me know in the comments.

00:14:40.505 --> 00:14:41.684
If there's another show
you want me to watch,

00:14:41.684 --> 00:14:43.795
please leave it down
below in the comments.

00:14:43.795 --> 00:14:45.678
The best the thing you
can do for this channel

00:14:45.678 --> 00:14:48.775
to help me make more content
to make better content

00:14:48.775 --> 00:14:51.745
is to subscribe and
then share this channel

00:14:51.745 --> 00:14:54.075
with your friends and family
so that they can subscribe.

00:14:54.075 --> 00:14:57.117
As always stay happy and healthy.

00:14:57.117 --> 00:14:59.700
(upbeat music)

